# component: toggle
# decisions: A11Y-12, API-5, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-5, FOC-6, FRM-4, TYP-18
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-[3px]
#     focus-visible:ring-ring/50` and the `aria-invalid` rings are removed.
#   FOC-5: the invalid border becomes `not-focus:aria-invalid:border-destructive`.
#   FRM-4: `disabled:pointer-events-none` is dropped, so a disabled toggle stays hoverable and a
#     Tooltip can explain why it is unavailable. Base UI's Toggle has no `focusableWhenDisabled`,
#     so the native `disabled` attribute stays — the pointer half of FRM-4 only.
#   API-5, A11Y-12: the `loading` prop, the out-of-flow spinner, and the label held at
#     `opacity-0` so the control's width does not move and its accessible name survives. The
#     label wrapper is an `inline-flex` box inheriting the root's `gap`, exactly as Button's is.
#     It shipped as `display: contents`, which generates NO box and therefore accepts no
#     `opacity`: the label painted at full strength UNDER the spinner for a full release, while
#     `toggle.test.tsx` asserted the `opacity-0` CLASS and passed. The compiled-CSS proof is in
#     `test/control-paint.browser.test.tsx` (ICO-8's sibling fix, 2026-09-22).
#   TYP-18: the `sm` tier's `text-[0.8rem]` becomes `text-xs`, matching Button's `sm` tier — the
#     two share a geometry (`h-7`, `px-2.5`) and must not disagree on type (MK, 2026-09-22).
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file; those hunks carry no decision of their own.
